# 3. USER ROLES AND PERMISSIONS

Implement secure role-based access control.

## A. Student

Students can:

- View their assigned grade, curriculum, subjects, and learning package.
- Access AI-generated lessons according to their subscription.
- Take quizzes and practice exercises.
- Attend assigned live classes.
- Access recorded lessons according to their plan.
- View homework, grades, attendance, and teacher feedback.
- Download permitted educational resources.
- Receive schedule reminders and learning notifications.
- View subscription status and expiration date.
- Request help from teachers when the relevant feature is available.

Students must never access another student's private information.

## B. Parent or guardian

Parents can:

- Register and manage their own account.
- Add and manage multiple children.
- View each child's grade, curriculum, subjects, and assigned plan.
- View progress, grades, homework, attendance, and teacher feedback.
- See upcoming classes and past sessions.
- Manage subscriptions and payment history.
- Receive payment reminders and class notifications.
- Update contact information.
- Request support.
- Request schedule changes where permitted.

A parent must only access children explicitly associated with their account.

## C. Teacher

Teachers are employees of EduCraft and receive fixed monthly salaries.

Teacher dashboards must include:

- Assigned classes.
- Weekly and monthly schedules.
- Student lists for assigned classes.
- Class attendance.
- Upcoming lessons.
- Homework creation and management.
- Grading and feedback tools.
- Educational resource uploads.
- Lesson preparation tools.
- Access to approved AI-generated lesson materials.
- Class notes and progress records.
- Notifications about timetable changes.
- A view of their employment and salary records where authorized.

Teachers must not be able to change subscription prices, grant themselves administrator privileges, or access unrelated students.

Salary information must be private and visible only to authorized personnel.

## D. Administrator

Administrators can manage:

- Student accounts.
- Parent accounts.
- Teacher accounts.
- Administrator permissions.
- School levels and grade levels.
- Curricula and subjects.
- Subscription plans and pricing.
- Payments and subscriptions.
- Teacher salaries.
- Teacher qualifications and availability.
- Class sizes and schedules.
- Recorded lessons.
- Educational resources.
- AI provider settings.
- Platform configuration.
- Notifications.
- Reports and analytics.
- Customer support.
