# 11. AUTOMATIC CLASS ASSIGNMENT

Build a scheduling and allocation engine.

Students should be assigned to appropriate classes automatically.

The system must consider:

- Student's school level.
- Grade.
- Curriculum.
- Subject.
- Language.
- Subscription plan.
- Number of remaining classes.
- Teacher qualifications.
- Teacher availability.
- Class capacity.
- Existing reservations.
- Time zone.
- Scheduling conflicts.
- Makeup-class eligibility.

Never assign a student to an incompatible grade, curriculum, or subject.

Never exceed the maximum class size for a student's plan.

For mixed-plan classes, enforce the strictest applicable class-size restriction. For example, if a class includes VIP students, the class must not exceed four students unless a separate class is created.

Do not double-book teachers or students.

If no appropriate class is available, place the student on a waiting list or notify the administrator. Never silently discard the assignment request.

Record why an assignment was made so administrators can investigate scheduling problems.

